    [344, "olympiadbench", "Let $x$ be a real number in the interval $[0,360]$ such that the four expressions $\\sin x^{\\circ}, \\cos x^{\\circ}$, $\\tan x^{\\circ}, \\cot x^{\\circ}$ take on exactly three distinct (finite) real values. Compute the sum of all possible values of $x$.", "990", [11745, 0, 1, "990", " \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} - 1}{2}\\right)\\) and \\(x_2 = 180^\\circ - x_1\\)\n   - Sum: \\(180^\\circ\\)\n\n3. **Case (F): \\(\\tan x = \\cot x\\)**\n   - Solutions: \\(x_1 = 135^\\circ\\) and \\(x_2 = 315^\\circ\\)\n   - Sum: \\(135^\\circ + 315^\\circ = 450^\\circ\\)\n\n### Total Sum:\n- Summing the contributions from all cases:\n  \\[\n  360^\\circ + 180^\\circ + 450^\\circ = 990^\\circ\n  \\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{990}\n\\]"], [12170, 0, 0, "810", "beta \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 360^\\circ - \\beta\n     \\]\n\n### Summing the Valid Solutions\n\n- \\( x = 135^\\circ \\)\n- \\( x = 315^\\circ \\)\n- \\( x = \\beta \\)\n- \\( x = 360^\\circ - \\beta \\)\n\nThe sum of these solutions is:\n\\[\n135^\\circ + 315^\\circ + \\beta + (360^\\circ - \\beta)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 135^\\circ + 315^\\circ + 360^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n= 810^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of all possible values of \\( x \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{810}\n\\]"], [10680, 0, 0, "450", "     - \\(\\sin 315^\\circ = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\), \\(\\cos 315^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\), \\(\\tan 315^\\circ = 1\\), \\(\\cot 315^\\circ = 1\\).\n     - Distinct values: \\(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\), \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\), 1.\n\n3. **Sum of All Possible Values**:\n   - The valid angles are \\( 135^\\circ \\) and \\( 315^\\circ \\).\n   - Sum: \\( 135^\\circ + 315^\\circ = 450^\\circ \\).\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{450}\n\\]"]],
