    [346, "olympiadbench", "Let $a, b, m, n$ be positive integers with $a m=b n=120$ and $a \\neq b$. In the coordinate plane, let $A=(a, m), B=(b, n)$, and $O=(0,0)$. If $X$ is a point in the plane such that $A O B X$ is a parallelogram, compute the minimum area of $A O B X$.", "44", [10231, 0, 1, "44", " 5\\) and \\(b = 6\\):\n     \\[\n     m = \\frac{120}{5} = 24 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad n = \\frac{120}{6} = 20\n     \\]\n     - The area calculation:\n       \\[\n       \\text{Area} = \\left| 5 \\cdot 20 - 6 \\cdot 24 \\right| = \\left| 100 - 144 \\right| = 44\n       \\]\n   - The same result is obtained for other pairs like (10, 12) and (20, 24).\n\nThus, the minimum area of the parallelogram \\(AOBX\\) is \\(\\boxed{44}\\)."], [10615, 0, 1, "44", "   a + b = 5 + 6 = 11, \\quad ab = 5 \\cdot 6 = 30, \\quad |a - b| = 1\n   \\]\n   Therefore,\n   \\[\n   \\frac{|5^2 - 6^2|}{5 \\cdot 6} = \\frac{|25 - 36|}{30} = \\frac{11}{30}\n   \\]\n   The area is:\n   \\[\n   120 \\cdot \\frac{11}{30} = 44\n   \\]\n\n   Other pairs such as \\((10, 12)\\), \\((20, 24)\\), etc., also yield the same minimum value.\n\nThus, the minimum area of the parallelogram \\(AO BX\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{44}\n\\]"], [7748, 0, 1, "44", "  \\frac{12^2 - 10^2}{12 \\cdot 10} = \\frac{144 - 100}{120} = \\frac{44}{120} = \\frac{11}{30} \\approx 0.3667\n  \\]\n  The area is \\(120 \\times \\frac{11}{30} = 44\\).\n\n- For \\(a = 5\\) and \\(b = 6\\):\n  \\[\n  \\frac{5^2 - 6^2}{5 \\cdot 6} = \\frac{25 - 36}{30} = \\frac{-11}{30} = 0.3667\n  \\]\n  The area is \\(120 \\times \\frac{11}{30} = 44\\).\n\nThus, the minimum area of the parallelogram \\(AOBX\\) is \\(\\boxed{44}\\)."]],
